"""Cross-Provider Contract & Integration Validation Tests — Phase 27.

Validates that Kubernetes and OpenStack providers consistently implement
the common Server Manager architecture contract.

Covers (per Phase 27 spec section 2):
  1.  Equivalent adapter contract behavior
  2.  Deterministic Canonical IDs for repeated identical input
  3.  Stable normalization of identical snapshots
  4.  Missing fields and unknown enum values
  5.  Missing metrics must not become zero
  6.  UNKNOWN must not become HEALTHY
  7.  Failed discovery must not produce fake successful inventory
  8.  Evidence and provenance must be preserved
  9.  Only supported DIRECT/DERIVED evidence may create canonical relationships
  10. No INFERRED/UNKNOWN relationships are promoted into factual edges
  11. Duplicate entities and relationships are handled consistently
  12. Partial success and provider errors remain distinguishable
  13. Health extraction is registered and dispatched correctly
  14. Existing Management API response contracts remain compatible

Does NOT force both providers to expose identical entity kinds or capabilities.
Asserts consistent contracts, not identical provider data.
"""
